SOAPBOX: DE K7SV
SOAPBOX: A lot of time was spent by the crew affecting repair to antennas, rotators and
SOAPBOX: antenna switching in weeks prior to the contest. All the antennas and rotators
SOAPBOX: except the top 40 OWA rotator worked well throughout the weekend.
SOAPBOX: It’s always cool to work 5band DXCC in a weekend. It was equally cool to work
SOAPBOX: WAZ on 40!
SOAPBOX: We’ve certainly seen better conditions on 160 and 80, especially the former.
SOAPBOX: 80 seemed to be better to Eu the second night, particularly to Scandinavia and
SOAPBOX: Russia. On the other hand it seemed much poorer to Asia the second night.
SOAPBOX: It’s
SOAPBOX: time to remove the lot of conifers that have grown in the midst of the 80 4SQ
SOAPBOX: since it was built a number of years ago, but it’s still quite effective.
SOAPBOX: We were pleased to have a couple of new ops join us for the weekend. One was
SOAPBOX: quite new to contesting. He was thrilled to work a Handful of juicy mults on 15
SOAPBOX: meters. Operating from a multi operator station can really help turn a budding
SOAPBOX: contester into a lifelong diehard!
SOAPBOX: The crew extends their gratitude to Steve and Caroline for hosting the crew for
SOAPBOX: the weekend. Likewise kudos to those who assisted with repairs and getting a
SOAPBOX: couple of beverages up just prior to the contest.
SOAPBOX: Now on to ARRL DX CW
